Appendix F: Compendium of Engineering Proposals and Critical Advice

(Derived from the strategic analysis, presented as a consolidated reference for programme decision-makers.)

Proposals

1. Decouple crewed landing from settlement power. Use LM-10 success for a 2029–2030 landing; gate reactor deployment on demonstrated ISRU power demand, not calendar year.
2. Run Chang’e-7 as a true binary-fork gate. Publish quantitative ice thresholds before launch; pre-commit to architecture redesign if No-Go.
3. Treat Chang’e-8 as TRL-6 validation, not TRL-9 operations. Instrument for failure modes (dust, thermal cycling, abrasion); success = failure catalogue.
4. Develop a China-led 500 kWe-class surface reactor in parallel to Russia’s Elena-AM. Target TRL-4 by 2030, TRL-6 by 2035, deployment 2038–2042.
5. Standardise Queqiao Constellation ICDs by 2027. Lower barriers for international payloads; force partner contribution asymmetry into the open.
6. Fund a dust-mitigation grand challenge separate from ECLSS. 3-year terrestrial exposure programme for seals, bearings, optics against simulant dust + thermal cycling.
7. Exploit Artemis restructuring tactically, not architecturally. Freeze the LM-10/Mengzhou/Lanyue configuration; resist scope creep; build reliability through repetition.

Critical Advice (Caveats)

· The 14-day night is non-negotiable physics. 68 kWe keeps lights on, not refineries; >500 kWe continuous needed for settlement.
· ISRU grams ≠ ISRU kilograms. Lab 1.57 g/min is 2.26 kg/day; an astronaut needs 3 kg/day; propellant needs tonnes. Scaling is 15–25 years.
· Russia is a schedule risk, not a capability multiplier. Luna-25 failure; Luna-26 already slipped; Elena-AM “almost ready” but autonomous build is unprecedented. Plan B essential.
· ECLSS breakthrough ≠ ECLSS solution. Tiangong’s photosynthesis is TRL-4; lunar ECLSS needs >98% closure, dust tolerance, 15+ years maturation.
· Chang’e-7 can kill the ISRU business case. A null result requires honest redesign, not PR spin. Prepare Phase 2 for the no-ice case now.
· Crewed landing ≠ permanence. All hardware for landing exists; the unyielding bottlenecks are power, ISRU, ECLSS. Avoid declaring a base prematurely.
· Coalition ≠ contribution. Partner count is legitimacy; engineering remains Chinese. The SCI stays 0.591 if solo burden persists.
· U.S. delays are tactical, not structural. Artemis window is real, but rushing beyond TRL readiness repeats old mistakes; muscle memory matters more.

